  "findings": [
    {
      "claim": "The design's row 1 says to retire retro debt from health because `metasystem receipt status` reports it. That is not true at this commit. The removed health check was the only production code that read the durable retro-debt register (memory/retro-debt.json, read through retrodebt.Open). Retire it, and an owed retro that an arc completion, goal split, gate obligation or run conclusion records is no longer reported anywhere. The register also no longer reconciles itself against new retro receipts. The change drops the obligation instead of moving where it is reported. The slice does not work without fixing this, because a recorded human-owed duty goes silent.",
      "evidence": "The diff removes checkRetroDebt (metasystem/internal/steward/health.go, previously around line 597) and the only production import of retrodebt in health.go. A search of the reviewed tree finds retrodebt.Raise in goal/verbs.go:2327, goal/split.go:510, gaterun/weight.go:435 and run/conclude.go:450, and no production call of retrodebt.Open. cmd/metasystem/receipt_verbs.go:45-92 (receiptStatus) runs receipt.Check (internal/receipt/receipt.go:592-636), which judges 'N receipts since the last retro' or 'N days since', and internal/receipt does not import retrodebt. TestOpenRetroDebtLeavesTheSeatHealthy calls retrodebt.Open itself, so it does not show that any user-facing command reports the debt.",
      "id": "RETRO-DEBT-LOSES-ITS-ONLY-READER",
      "material": true,
      "severity": "medium"
    },
    {
      "claim": "On a checkout where seats are off (launch.seat.runtime=off, the default) and claimable work is waiting, session-main now reads dead with the false reason 'starting a seat for <goal>' and claims a lawful automatic remedy (hasLawfulAutomaticRemedy now returns true for every dead session-main). The tick never runs that remedy, because the seat ladder's first guard, SeatAllowed, refuses on such a checkout. So the red that someone can act on is delayed four observations behind AUTO_HEAL_ELIGIBLE. It names a repair that never happens. And the next unit's standing rule, which only catches dead roles with no lawful remedy, will never file it as a defect. Before this commit the same state read honestly: 'no session main is announced', NO_LAWFUL_REMEDY, alert at once. This goes against the goal's intent that a red is either acted on by the machinery or reaches a person.",
      "evidence": "Reproduced with a throwaway test in the temp copy: seat bed with seatReadyGoal(\"alpha\"), launcher.off set. checkSessionMainWithLedger gave status=dead, reason 'ready work has no seat; starting a seat for alpha', hasLawfulAutomaticRemedy=true. bed.tick(deadWorkers) gave action=notify, verdict=idle-backlog-dead, seat=nil, 0 starts. applyHealthObservation gave FailureEscalation=AUTO_HEAL_ELIGIBLE, ShouldAlert=false. Code path: health.go:490 calls checkSessionMainWithLedger with defaultSeatDependencies(nil), so there is no launcher and SeatAllowed is never asked. health.go:1146 calls PlanSeat directly. health.go:809 has 'case RoleStewardRunner, RoleSessionMain: return true'. seat_start.go:347-352 shows decideSeat returning ok=false when SeatAllowed is false. config/defaults.go:338 sets launch.seat.runtime to SeatRuntimeOff by default. health.go:770-781 suppresses the alert while a role is AUTO_HEAL_ELIGIBLE.",
